<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jericho</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jericho is a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-bank">West Bank</a> near the Jordan River, north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dead-sea">Dead Sea</a>, and one of the oldest continuously inhabited places in the world, with settlement at Tell es-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> from about 9000 BCE. Its springs and palm groves made it a royal estate under the Hasmoneans and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-the-great">Herod the Great</a>, who built winter palaces there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jericho.jpg" alt="Jericho" width="320" height="202" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fullo88 at Italian Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tell_es-sultan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
